;; The mutate<->judge pairing registry (pairing-as-data, notes/ADRs.md
;; ADR-0088; the design pass ruled AR-PD-0..6, review P3-3 D-3/D7-5): per-
;; operator WITNESSED rows -- inject defect class X, expect finding class X,
;; checked by execution instead of prose. A row lands only when this session
;; actually ran the loop (mutate -> gate -> observe) against a real fixture;
;; unwitnessed operator x judge cells simply do not appear here (ADR-0088's
;; own tier-two coverage table records which cells that leaves open, report-
;; only). Loaded and schema-validated by `ehrt.judge.pairing/load-registry`.
;;
;; :locator is this registry's own addition to the row shape the design pass
;; named (:operator/:judge/:expected/:fixture/:witness) -- every v2 operator
;; here is `:locator-required? true` (ehrt.corpus.operators), so a row that
;; does not carry its own replay locator cannot actually be replayed by the
;; tier-one per-row test; disclosed in ADR-0088 rather than silently added.
;;
;; :expected is the set of finding CLASSES this session observed becoming
;; NEW (present in the mutant's findings, absent or less frequent in the
;; unmutated baseline's own findings) after applying :operator at :locator
;; and gating through :judge -- for judge-v2-hapi, the finding's own :code
;; (the raising HAPI exception's kebab-cased class name); for judge-v2-nist,
;; the finding's own :category (a name drawn from the engine's reference.conf
;; taxonomy, judge-v2-nist/resources/judge-v2-nist/taxonomy.edn -- schema-
;; checked, see judge-v2-nist's own currency-gate test).
;;
;; :profile is a second, judge-v2-nist-only addition (optional key): the
;; conformance-profile bundle directory judge-v2-nist/make-validator needs
;; alongside :fixture -- a base-structural (judge-v2-hapi) row needs no
;; profile at all, so this key is absent there rather than always-present.
